<title>USA: State Street CEO increases stock holdings.</title>
<headline>State Street CEO increases stock holdings.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>State Street Corp said Friday that Marshall Carter, its chairman and chief executive, had done a cashless exercise of stock options, thereby increasing his direct ownership of the company's stock by 38,800 shares.</p>
<p>After the transactions, Carter owns 123,410 shares, State Street said.</p>
<p>State Street services and manages financial assets worldwide and has over $3 trillion in assets under custody and over $350 billion under management.</p>
</text>
